 "notes": "Words by Josephine V. Rowe; music by Harold R. White, published under the name Dermot MacMurrough (1910). \"Macushla\" is the Irish mo chuisle, \"my pulse\", i.e. my darling. Recorded famously by John McCormack. IPA follows sung British English: non-rhotic (r sounded only before a vowel, as a light flip [r]), no stress marks on one-syllable words. The gloss line restates archaic or poetic words in plain modern English."
